[{:db/id 17592186133734 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-92b0451f-5a0f-52d2-ba64-98d0de8b76eb" "question-b5496cbf-43fd-56ac-8687-6111e219fb1f" "question-44cc42c9-2404-5dbe-b1d3-8cf7bb1969eb" "question-e84b722e-1f7b-5e51-918b-729f6c73a9a8" "question-26ac2004-f968-51f4-b0b0-b14b01861ad2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133507 :question/problem "Calculate the value of $7^2.$" :question/worked-solution "To work out $7^2,$ we multiply $7$ by itself:\n\n$$\n7^2 = 7 \\cdot 7 = 49\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133735 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8752fb1d-1037-5b8f-989d-db4a62d747cd" "question-5df64b77-ebca-5b73-8314-1b0b4f096670" "question-0aa077c8-b467-563f-9ed3-1a4e44b467f3" "question-28839411-a8dd-5863-a44c-b7b61fd48e0a" "question-a5930e78-0883-51ee-8797-7a8e907a4b0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133508 :question/problem "Find the square of $\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To work out $\\left(\\dfrac 1 2\\right)^2,$ we multiply $\\dfrac 1 2$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac 1 2\\right)^2 = \\dfrac 1 2 \\cdot \\dfrac 1 2 = \\dfrac 1 4\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133736 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fa89591c-42d2-57e3-bfd4-69e840192bd4" "question-397f8e4c-8a02-58fc-a48a-6b5a482557f8" "question-63757b4a-7f76-56b7-8980-04eae99b6886" "question-f5d1c8d9-881c-5cab-bdcb-86d5598dd1ea" "question-668fdcb5-56eb-5d4c-8344-17b223fde624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133509 :question/problem "What is the value of $(-4)^2?$" :question/worked-solution "To work out $(-4)^2,$ we multiply $-4$ by itself:\n\n$$\n(-4)^2 = (-4) \\cdot (-4) = 16\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-28d7dd84-346e-5b73-9ead-af1c62abb54d" "question-f176b794-be06-5dbc-b5c3-35aaeec4668c" "question-c5bedd10-8ffa-5ad9-bdb2-5aa9ca8ef32b" "question-58bd0ac9-9ea6-5ce8-9fc3-fc8a73b17344" "question-e04ccdd3-f28d-58f9-a502-15fb5e93205e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133510 :question/problem "What is the square of $-2.5?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to calculate the product of $(-2.5)$ with itself:\n\n$$\n(-2.5)^2 = (-2.5)\\cdot (-2.5) = (2.5)\\cdot (2.5)\n$$\n\nFirst, we ignore the decimal points and multiply as if both numbers were whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\color{blue}1[/math]}} \\\\ \\boxed{\\text{[math]\\color{blue}2[/math]}}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $25 \\times 25 =   625.$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $\\color{blue}1$ decimal place in the first factor ($2.5$) and $\\color{blue}1$ decimal place in the second factor ($2.5$), so their product will have ${\\color{blue}{1}} + {\\color{blue}{1}} = 2$ decimal places.\n\nWe take our value of $625$ and insert a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places:\n\n![](images/9f/9f3292917fa7500519b6e0fe1232b414189b00601d56107fc2643990e814c09f.svg)\n\nTherefore, $(-2.5)^2 = 6.25\\,.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-92b0451f-5a0f-52d2-ba64-98d0de8b76eb" :question/id #uuid "92b0451f-5a0f-52d2-ba64-98d0de8b76eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-185072" :question/problem "${7}^{2}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution